🔺 Python Character Pyramid Generator

A simple Python program that generates a centered pyramid pattern using a user-selected character. The pyramid height is controlled by an odd number entered by the user.

This project demonstrates basic Python concepts such as loops, input validation, and pattern generation.

📌 Description

This script allows the user to:

Enter the maximum width of the pyramid (must be an odd number)

Choose a character to build the pyramid

Automatically generate a centered pyramid using the chosen character

The program uses Python’s built-in features along with the re module (imported for potential input validation extension).

⚙️ Features

✅ Generates a symmetric pyramid pattern

✅ User-defined pyramid size

✅ User-selected character

✅ Automatically centers the pyramid

✅ Beginner-friendly and easy to understand

🛠 Requirements

Python 3.x

No external libraries required

🚀 How to Run

Save the code in a file, for example:

pyramid.py


Run the program in the terminal or command prompt:

python pyramid.py

🧠 Example Usage
enter the maximum number of characters in the pyramid: 7
enter the character for pyramid: *

      *
    * * *
  * * * * *
* * * * * * *

📖 How It Works

The program follows these steps:

Prompts the user to enter the maximum pyramid width

Ensures the number is odd for proper symmetry

Prompts the user to enter a character

Uses nested loops to:

Print spaces for alignment

Print characters to form the pyramid shape

Displays the pyramid in the console

🧩 Code Structure

main() – Controls program flow

Input handling – Collects pyramid size and character

Loop logic – Builds pyramid rows

Output formatting – Aligns pyramid correctly

⚠️ Limitations

Only works with odd numbers

Runs in the command line (no GUI)

Does not currently validate character length (multiple characters allowed)

